The raw folder contains excel spreadsheets unchanged as received from the spreadsheets.
The processed folder contains these data parsed (manually) ready for input into the optimization pipeline.
In general this simply involves:
1) Matching the glucose assay to the corresponding cell-counts data.
2) Reformatting the glucose/fluorescence data into a single csv file.
3) Extracting the calibration data and saving into a separate file.

For details on how these objects are integrated into the workflow, see scripts/preliminaries_and_metadata.Rmd